Exp-11b:CardLayout

Aim: To write a Java program to demonstrate CardLayout.

Algorithm:
1. Start the program.
2. Import the AWT package.
3. Create a Frame.
4. Create a CardLayout object.
5. Create a Panel and set CardLayout.
6. Add three buttons as separate cards.
7. Display the first card.
8. Stop the program.
Program:

File name: CardLayoutExample.java
import java.awt.*;

public class CardLayoutExample {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Frame f = new Frame("Card Layout");

        CardLayout cl = new CardLayout();
        Panel p = new Panel();

        p.setLayout(cl);

        p.add(new Button("Card 1"), "First");
        p.add(new Button("Card 2"), "Second");
        p.add(new Button("Card 3"), "Third");

        f.add(p);

        f.setSize(300, 200);
        f.setVisible(true);
    }
}


Output:









Only one card is displayed at a time. The other cards remain hidden until selected through CardLayout operations.

Result: Thus, the Java program to demonstrate CardLayout was executed successfully.
